Z||000006||Nashco||03-17-2001||05:25 PM||||Loki, here's a way I've seen work, hopefully it'll work for you.  Just find a bolt that has the same width as the square drive.  In your case, this will be a bolt with a 5/16" hex head. Obviously, this won't fit in the hole because of the two hex points that stick past the square edges.  Take the bolt head to a grinder/cut-off tool and remove those two edges that won't fit.  This will create a...well...it should be close to square, depending on how hard you tried    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Anyway, then get two nuts that fit the thread of the bolt.  Tighten these two bolts against each other a ways down the shaft.  This should create a hex nut in between the head and the nut on the end that you can turn (remember, righty tight lefty loosy) and remove the plug.  This should help if there's any confusion:<P>  <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/jbnash/squaredrive.gif">  <P>Good luck!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>            <BR>P.S.  ASCII drawings don't work in this the forum...now I know <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 03-17-2001).]||||reg||1
