Z||000008||Loki||03-17-2001||07:27 PM||||OK got another question....Does it matter which head the sensor goes on? Cause on the back side (by firewall) the plug there acctually has a bolt head on it.....?????<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||03-17-2001||08:33 PM||||for starters, all the bolts and nuts are metric unless someones messed with them. if your saying your plug has a square or hex recess in the top, just go to hardware store and get a small set of hex keys that fits your 3/8 drive rachet. there not that expensive for a cheap set. chances are youll need them some day again. I got a set of 20 at sears for $12.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Loki||03-17-2001||08:44 PM||||Only thing is..No one has a squre thing that will fit on the ratchet.....Will a hex work in a square opening?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||My7Fieros||03-17-2001||09:13 PM||||I dont think Im following your question. <BR>It takes a 5/16 socket...DEEP WELL. When you buy the socket, itll either have a 1/4, 3/8, or 1/2 inch drive (aka the "square thing")...its not rocket science. These are the only three sizes there are. If your ratchet has a different size drive on it (like if your ratchet is a 1/2 inch drive, and the socket has a 3/8 size opening) then buy an adapter)...<BR>M7F||||reg||1
Z||000012||Loki||03-17-2001||09:19 PM||||Nope your not following....<BR>  The "PLug" Has what appears to be a 5/16 size recessed opening...Like a socket...(Wish I had a camera) I need a 5/16 extention for the ratchet...Picture a socket with threads as the plug......<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Nashco||03-17-2001||09:54 PM||||Oh my gosh Loki...I thought that would have been clear enough.  Actually, I thought I'd overkilled it.  I know what you're talking about!!!  I've rebuilt motors before, not like I'm new to plugs either...sheesh.  The instructions were to get a hex head bolt and grind two corners off so that IT IS SQUARE!  So once you've ground the bolt head so it can fit into the SQUARE HOLE then you can put two nuts on the bolt.  If you tighten the nuts against each other, you can use one of the nuts to TURN THE BOLT WITH THE SQUARE HEAD.  This is basically like a socket with a square head, except you've made it with a bolt and a nut instead of casting it.  THE BOLT HAS A SQUARE HEAD!  YOU MACHINE A HEXAGONAL BOLT TO BE SQUARE...GRIND THE CORNERS THAT DON'T FIT UNTIL THE BOLT FITS.  Whew...I'm hoping now that I typed it in caps you heard me right  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Hex head + square hole = no good<BR>Square head + square hole = good<P>Just remember, the only difference between a hexagon and a square is two corners.  You are allowed to make tools.  It's actually very useful to make tools for some jobs.  Keep this in mind.  Think outside the box.  There is a tool you can buy for this, but it'll cost ya 5 bucks and you'll use it one time.<P>I'm just trying to help...I think you totally misunderstood the instructions.  SQUARE...THINK SQUARE!<P>Making sense now?<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 03-17-2001).]||||reg||11
Z||000014||Loki||03-17-2001||10:53 PM||||OK, I did understand you then......   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Just have to fond a grinder...Ill get it eventually<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
